{"title":"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(recommended)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (recommended)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Hard)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Hard)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Formula)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Formula)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An equilateral triangle and a regular hexagon have equal perimeters. If the triangle's area is 4, what is the area of the hexagon?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/e/47e97b6ce1877b8841935688be31d2ab7dbcb776.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\hspace{.05in}4\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\hspace{.05in}5\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\hspace{.05in}6\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\hspace{.05in}4\\sqrt3\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\hspace{.05in}6\\sqrt3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"400\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28recommended.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(recommended)\">Solution 1 (recommended)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (recommended)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the perimeter of the equilateral triangle be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/8/f28de6b767ea937f3cfc80afb5bb23fb903a9964.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3s$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />. The side length of the equilateral triangle would then be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> and the sidelength of the hexagon would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/3/c5372e4a6aa030c5c2973cc7aad79bad38f9241b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{s}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"33\" />.\n</p><p>A hexagon contains six equilateral triangles. One of these triangles would be similar to the large equilateral triangle in the ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/7/7a7fb95082673f1d3c7a82fdd28d1c54319f8444.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 : 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" />, since the sidelength of the small equilateral triangle is half the side length of the large one. Thus, the area of one of the small equilateral triangles is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The area of the hexagon is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/8/7280bf8368c04ac2c82dc3f7967b903252cb868f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\times 6 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"119\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Hard.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Hard)\">Solution 2 (Hard)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Hard)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the side length of the small triangle be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec701493fa72dda5d6747fe14f30e7b1c2fb6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />, so the side length of the hexagon is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. By the Pythagorean theorem, the height of the triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/f/00fc45eea294781fdd51408a9373e4b36eac70dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" />, so the area of the triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/8/9a8b8981b6b98159e712761fbfc95d049ca2cf6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x^2}{\\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"30\" height=\"45\" /> We are given that the area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so x must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/5/885e153e1a083a72a7d086ce523df4274c2a6e20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[4]{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"31\" height=\"43\" />. Therefore, by the Pythagorean theorem, the height of one of the triangles in the hexagon (made by subdividing the hexagon into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> congruent triangles), is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/b/7fb564a7492adc5383c559d3d8434b98f9aef138.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt[4]{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"31\" height=\"48\" />, so the area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/3/9d31761dddd4fdabbc0cfb25a0dd6a7e788d54fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[4]{3}}\\times\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt[4]{3}}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"75\" height=\"48\" />, which equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Since there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> such triangles in the hexagon, the area of the hexagon is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/3/a536e34c10b022c7892c89afd52a136d7a61695d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"56\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Formula.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Formula)\">Solution 3 (Formula)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Formula)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The area of an equilateral triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/b/bbbe9248655083c594723e2e8b182bd7d1eb6c38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} a^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"47\" height=\"43\" />, where a is the side. Since a hexagon is six equilateral triangles combined, the area of a hexagon is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/7/af79810b6cb311c7008fea57875bd77963e6eeb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right) a^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"87\" height=\"55\" />. If we assume the side of the hexagon is 1, and the side of the triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />(perimeter is the same but sides are 6:3), then the area of the triangle will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/b/a9bddfa0dd561449e70720e765113a3c75dc6382.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"21\" />. We killed it is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/1/f1189b63cdef76572dedacf2da217353560012f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{3} : 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"21\" /> ratio of the assumed triangle area to the actual triangle area. This indicates the area of the hexagon will also be a ratio of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/1/f1189b63cdef76572dedacf2da217353560012f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{3} : 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"21\" />, so the area of the assumed hexagon is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/1/1b1cd991e4fe587a918dff181a824ed877790235.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"35\" height=\"41\" />. Therefore, the area of the actual hexagon will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/9/a2901d8a2501f9df64f90bfecc191d9f49e8f35c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\cdot 4}{\\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"56\" height=\"50\" />. Simplifying the result will give us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/3/a536e34c10b022c7892c89afd52a136d7a61695d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"56\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/SctoIY1cbss\">https://youtu.be/SctoIY1cbss</a> ~pi is 3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by\">Video Solution by</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/j3QSD5eDpzU?t=2101\">https://youtu.be/j3QSD5eDpzU?t=2101</a>\n</p><p>~ WhyMath\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8\" title=\"2012 AMC 8\">2012 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2012\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_8_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 8 Problems and Solutions\"> All AJHSME/AMC 8 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016233541\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.049 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.064 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 215/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2272/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 132/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5295/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.618      1 -total\n 58.33%    8.527      1 Template:AMC8_box\n 39.07%    5.711      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:11569:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261016233541 and revision id 284967. Rendering was triggered because